        }
      },
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_ObxJgm8y",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_O_OK2enY"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_3GeAl0Gj",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Let's start by looking at the overall storage architecture of OpenMAIC. This diagram gives us a high‑level view of how the system is organized."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_rBViy0b2",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_2gOrYT_J"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_60B4qr_o",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "First, we have three key storage modules: the Disk module for persistent data, the Cache layer for fast, temporary access, and the Metadata component that tracks where everything lives."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_4owR5XKD",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "chart__VmA6He4"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_8OCR4CK7",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "The chart illustrates the data flow between these modules. Data is written to disk, cached for quick reads, and metadata coordinates the lookup—ensuring the system remains both durable and responsive."
        }
      ],
      "createdAt": 1777971162851,
      "updatedAt": 1777971162851
    },
