        },
        {
          "id": "action_9yuVIgPN",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Let's walk through the step‑by‑step smoke test procedure for OpenMAIC storage."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_bUt6RWn1",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_N3hx32Ny"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_xP2phO-7",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "First, we need to prepare the test environment—make sure the storage service is up, configuration files are in place, and any required test data is seeded."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_cbsHkHhA",
          "type": "laser",
          "elementId": "text_N3hx32Ny"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_d9RW1SIZ",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Next, run the built‑in smoke‑test command provided by OpenMAIC. It's a single CLI call that exercises the core storage APIs."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_sZWUyP8R",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_4XpG_NfW"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_X3DLljvp",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Finally, interpret the result report: a green status means all health checks passed, while any red entries point to specific failures you can investigate."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_y3x-fVNc",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Any questions about these steps before we move on to a live demonstration?"
        }
      ],
